1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Îro emê bi hev re gundekî din nas bikin, gundê Xilalka.
 
Today we will get to know another village together, the
village of Xilalka.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Ev gundê Xilalka jî girêdayî navçeya Bilbilê,
 
This village of Xilalka is also connected to the Bulbule
district,

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
di quntara Çiyayê Gazê da hatiye avakirin,
 
It was built at the foothills of Mount Gaze,

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Emê bi hev re derbasî gund bibin, emê bi hev re nas bikin.
 
We will enter the village together, we will get to know it
together.

5
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Di her gundekî da taybetmendiyeke xwe heye,
 
Every village has its own feature,

6
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Bi rastî jî taybetmendiya vî gundî heye,
 
Actually this village has a feature,

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Elê rojava ye Kurdistanê, hemî gundên, min ev taybetmendiya
nedî.
 
In all the villages of Rojava Kurdistan, I haven't seen this
feature.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Niha emê bi hev re derbas bibin, emê bi hev re nas bikin,
taybetmendiya vî gundî çiye.
 
Now we will go inside together, we will get to know together
what the feature of this village is.

9
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Em li ser van keviran rûnin.
 
We sit on these stones.

10
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, di vî gundî da jî kevir di ber
dîwaran de,
 
Yes, dear viewers, in this village too there are stones
along the walls,

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Her kevirek jî ê malbatekê ye.
 
And every stone belongs to a family.

12
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Dema mêvanekî vî gundî derbas dibe,
 
When a guest enters this village,

13
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Tê li ser van keviran rûdinê.
 
They come and sit on these stones.

14
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Ew xwediyê kevir kî ye, ew tê mêvanê xwe pêşwazî dike.
 
Whoever the owner of the stone is, he comes to welcome his
guest.

15
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Niha jî em li benda li gund bin, em binêrin ev kevrê kî
amadene niha rûniştine.
 
Now let's wait in the village, let's see whose stones are
ready for sitting.

16
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Wey ehlen we sehlen, ser çavên me.
 
Wow, welcome, on our eyes.

17
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Merheba Xalo.
 
Hello uncle.

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Wey ehlen we sehlen.
 
Wow welcome.

19
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Ehlen we sehlen ser çava, merheba.
 
Welcome, on our eyes, hello.

20
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:15,000
De kerem kin rûnin.
 
Please sit down.

21
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Xalo spas dikim ji te ra.
 
Uncle, I thank you.

22
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Ser çavê min bi xêr hatin.
 
On my eyes, welcome.

23
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Em îro mêvanê gundê we ne.
 
We are guests of your village today.

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Wey ehlen we sehlen.
 
Wow, welcome.

25
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Di gund da behs dikirin, digotin taybetmendiyek me heye.
 
In the village they were talking about it and saying we have
a feature.

26
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Digotin di gund da kevir hene.
 
They were saying there are stones in the village.

27
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

28
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Digot her mêvanekî me tê derbasî ser kevran rûdinê,
 
They said every guest of ours comes and sits on the stones,

29
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Ew xwediyê kevir kî be ew mêvanî pêşwazî dike.
 
Whoever the owner of the stone is, they will welcome that
guest.

30
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Welleh em nizanin bîstî jî, tarîxa ya'nî bav û kalên me da
ev tişt heye.
 
By God we don't know exactly, it's in the history of our
ancestors.

31
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Ji kevn da ye?
 
Is it from old times?

32
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Kevn da ye. Nahat bîrî kesî. Emrî min ya'nî şêst û heft sal
e, berî min da dibêjin çil sal e ev niza bû.
 
It's from old times. Nobody remembers. My age is 67, they
say this has existed 40 years before me.

33
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Ya Apo Hecî ev taybetmendiya bes di vî gundî da te dîye.
 
Oh Uncle Haci, have you only seen this feature in your
village?

34
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Îşte ev bav û kalên me jî, çêkirin. Mal hindik bûne wê çaxê,
 
Actually our ancestors made it. Houses were few at that
time,

35
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Êdî bav û kalan gotî werin, mêvanên me hatin, kîjan ser
kevrî kî ye, em kê bin.
 
So the ancestors said come, our guests came, whoever comes
on whose stone, we'll take them.

36
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Mêvan kî hat ser kevrî rûnişt em ê gund, am kî ban ew li ser
kevrê wan da diçû, paşê te dibirin mal.
 
Whose guest came and sat on the stone, they belonged to the
village, they would go to their stone, then they would take
them home.

37
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Îşte baş e adetek xwe wena çêkiribûn. Heta derkî paşê, nav
lê dan kevrê mêra.
 
Actually they had made such a good tradition. Later they
named them stones of men.

38
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Aa vêra digotin kevrê mêra?
 
Ah, did they call this the stones of men?

39
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

40
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Çima ev nav lê kirin?
 
Why did they give it this name?

41
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Mêr lê rûniştin, wê demê şore da, ev nav lê kirin.
 
Men used to sit on it at that time, they gave it this name.

42
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Ê mêvanên çaxê ku dihatin, ji kîjan gundî pirtir dihatin?
 
From which village did the guests come more?

43
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Ê mêvanê ku nizanîbû kê dîtiye wekî îro na.
 
The guest who didn't know who they saw, not like today.

44
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Dê wê demê da mêvan pir bûn, hendik bûn dihatin?
 
Were the guests at that time many or few coming?

45
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Ê na pir bûn, na wekî niha nîn e.
 
Oh no, they were many, not like now.

46
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Dê wê demê da makîne, erebeyan tinebû.
 
Since cars didn't exist at that time.

47
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Na na tiştek tinebû.
 
No, no there was nothing.

48
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Bi meşê dihat. Şûna erebê da.. hatin bi erebe meşiya bûn.
 
They came walking. Instead of a car.. they used to walk.

49
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Naha dema mêvanek dihat dizanibû kîjan kevre, kîjan malê ye,
yan nedizanî?
 
Now when a guest came, did he know whose stone it is, whose
house it is, or didn't he know?

50
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Ser kîjan rûdinişt ê wî nedizanî.
 
On whichever he sat, he didn't know.

51
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Te nizanî kevrê mêra, yê mala şêx e.
 
You don't know the men's stone is of the sheikh's house.

52
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Ew xwedanê wê malê kî ye aîleyek ew e dihat mal. Tu dibirî
mal.
 
Whoever is the owner of that house, they would take him
home. You would take him home.

53
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Bi çi xwestek te heye, encama kî derê, wî derî ji te ra
dihat hiştin.
 
Whatever request you have, whatever place it is, his door
was left open for you.

54
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Îşê adetên wisa avahî weha çêkiribûn.
 
That's why they had built such customs.

55
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Yanî naha ez hatim, min mala wî nizanî, ez hatim li ser
kevran...
 
So now I came, whose house I don't know, I came to a
stone...

56
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Ew dertê tê da, de.. te dît de te bibe.
 
He comes out, he.. he sees you and takes you.

57
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Kê mala kê dixwast de tu diçûyî der wî... çi kar hebû paşê
de diçû di.
 
Whoever wanted whose house you would go there... whatever
work there was.. he would go.

58
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Ya'nî edetî wa wisa çêbû bûn.
 
You know, those traditions were formed like this.

59
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Apo Hecî emrê te çiqas e?
 
Uncle Haci, how old are you?

60
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Heftê û şeş e..
 
It is seventy-six..

61
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Gundî çiqas e li bazara...
 
How much did the village go to the market...

62
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Zêdetir dikirin kilîsê...
 
They mostly went to Kilis...

63
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Tu jî çûyî kilîsê te jî dî?
 
Did you also go to Kilis and see it?

64
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Na min ne dî ye, min negihaştiyê.
 
No, I haven't seen it, I didn't reach it.

65
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Ez tiştekî ji te bipirsim kerem ke.
 
Let me ask you something, please.

66
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Kaniyên ku te dibêje tenê di gund da me, caran şaşî çêdibin,
gava ev mêvan dihat, dihat ser kevir rûniştî kî pêşwazî
dikir?
 
The springs that you say are only in the village, sometimes
we make mistakes, when this guest came, sat on a stone, who
would welcome him?

67
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Na di wê çaxê dema mêvanek dihat, gava ku mêvan ser kîjan
kevrî rûnişt dî we ye malbatê ye.
 
No, at that time when a guest came, whenever the guest sat
on which stone, it belonged to the family.

68
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Malbat jî di wê demê da çend aîla yek navsikirin... her
kevrek yê malbatê ke di nav de..
 
The family at that time used to call several families as
one... every stone belonged to a family in it..

69
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Ser kîjan kevrî rûnişt wê, xwediyê wî kevrê ye aîla wê ye...
 
Whoever sat on whichever stone, the owner of that stone is
its family...

70
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Aîlê me yek bû ya'nî, pênç şeş heft pismam bûn... ev aîla
evrê ne bûn.
 
Our family was one, you know, five, six, seven cousins...
they were not the family here.

71
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Gava dihatin ser vî kevrî diketin, mêvan dibirin mal.
 
When they came and fell on this stone, they would take the
guest home.

72
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Xizmeta vî mêvanî wacib e, vî mêvanî çibî temam dikirin
daxwaza vî çi bû, dixwest diçû bi kê da dipirsî da...
 
The service of this guest is obligatory, whatever this guest
needed they fulfilled it, whatever his request was, he
wanted he went and asked whoever...

73
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Wê çaxê ez mecbûr im ez, kesê ku li ser kevrê min rûniştîye
ez vî pêşwazî bikim.
 
At that time I am obliged, the person who sat on my stone,
to welcome him.

74
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Karê wî çi ye, xwestekê wî çi ye temam wê ez amade bikim vî
mêvanî bi dilşadî.
 
Whatever his job is, his request is, okay I will prepare it
for this guest with happiness.

75
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Ev taybetmenda vî gundî ye. Gundekî wek Xilalka.
 
This is the feature of this village. A village like Xilalka.

76
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Ez geştiya me... ev der gundê me da darek mezin lê bû.
 
I have traveled... this place in our village had a big tree.

77
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Ev dara ketin.. ama wek dar kî piçûk lê ketin sa ra sax e..
 
This tree fell.. but like a small tree they fell on it, it's
alive..

78
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:01,000
E ketin der ginda bûn...
 
They fell outside they were...

79
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Ê tu gundî te gundî dî jî hene le taybet ne dîye...
 
You are a villager, you have other villages but you haven't
seen this special...

80
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:14,000
E xwedî emrê min 53 sal e min li tu gundek de ne dî me,
rastî ne min milên Efrîn, ne milên Kobanê ne mil Cizîrê.
 
Look, I am 53 years old, I have not seen it in any village,
truly I haven't seen it in Afrin side, nor Kobane side, nor
Cizire side.

81
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Ev taybetmendiye nîne..
 
This feature doesn't exist.

82
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Îşte vê derê emê ji zarokê me yê piçûk jî bipirse dê bêje
kevrê mêra, her kes dizane.
 
So here even if we ask our little child he will say the
stone of men, everyone knows.

83
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Kevrê mêra.
 
Stone of men.

84
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Bes vê derê berê xweş bû, makîne hat xera kir...
 
But this place used to be nice, a car came and ruined it...

85
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Ew darên dirêj tew yek tê de nîn in, teva rabûn...
 
Those tall trees, not even one is in it, all of them fell...

86
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Ez ji te xatir xwestin daxwazim..
 
I request to bid you farewell..

87
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Em ne mecbûrên mêvan in wext bî...
 
We are not obliged to guests if there is time...

88
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Ez de biçim gerim ez spas bo te dikim..
 
I will go around, I thank you..

89
00:07:51,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Ehlen we sehlen...
 
Welcome...

90
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Merheba Şêxê Mihemed.
 
Hello Sheikh Mihemed.

91
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Merheba ser çavan.
 
Hello, on eyes.

92
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Spas ji te ra..
 
Thank you..

93
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Îro mêvanê gundê we ne, gundê Xilalka ne, ez ji te dixwazim
em navê gund bipirsin..
 
Today we are guests of your village, the village of Xilalka,
I want to ask you the name of the village..

94
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Ser çava ew ser dilê me rabuwe...
 
On eyes he has risen on our heart...

95
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Em hûn hatin li ser bernameyeke şêrîn de pêşwazî bikin..
 
We came to welcome you on a sweet program..

96
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Pîroz dikin wê. Xizmet û rize wêra...
 
You are celebrating it. Service and respect to you...

97
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Navê Xilalka du gotin hene. Yek ji xelala avê...
 
The name Xilalka has two meanings. One is from the water
spring...

98
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Gelek av li aliyê rojavayê gundê Xilalka heye... Av xelal
e.. Av cûda ye...
 
There is a lot of water on the west side of Xilalka
village... The water is pure.. Water is different...

99
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Wek dibînim ew zinar li bin e, li geliyekê wexta baran
dibare av di bin zinar da digere..
 
As I see that rock is underneath, in a valley when it rains,
water goes under the rock..

100
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Dîrokek me da dibêje av li bin wî zinarî re diçe..
 
From our history it says water goes under that rock..

101
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Ew dibêjin Xilal av derbas dibe.. di gundê Xilalka de ye...
 
They say Xilal water passes through.. it's in Xilalka
village...

102
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Yanî ev du wate li vir hene, yek navê Xilalka tê wateya encî
av tê ji van zinaran re tê bin...
 
So there are two meanings here, one is the name Xilalka
means that water comes from under these rocks...

103
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Xilal Osmanlî kir Sulaqlî... Sû av e.
 
Xilal was translated to Sulaqli by the Ottomans... Su is
water.

104
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Ev Erebî hat terîbkirin, gotinên Erebî hatin kirin, navê avê
ye.
 
This Arabic was arabicized, Arabic words were made, it's the
name of water.

105
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Ê ev wateyê wê heye.
 
Yes, it has this meaning.

106
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Osmanî jî li gorî xwe dan û ereban jî xwe dan...
 
The Ottomans also named it in their way and the Arabs in
their way...

107
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:55,000
E bi Tirkî me'nê de, av e...
 
It means in Turkish, it is water...

108
00:09:55,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Gundê Xilalka çiqas mal in?
 
How many houses are there in Xilalka village?

109
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Te behsa salên wî kir ya 400 sal hatiye, bi baweriya min be
na. Gundê Xelalka lewma malbat, malek xera kirin,
 
You mentioned its age, saying it dates back 400 years, but
in my opinion, no. The village of Xelalka, because a family
destroyed a house,

110
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:15,000
zîvek li bin stûnê derket. Emrê wî zîvî 750 sal bû.
 
a silver piece came out from under a pillar. The age of that
silver piece was 750 years.

111
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:21,000
Vêca bitalî 750 sal dem ek pere derkeve, maneto gund ji wê
pirr bêtir kevnetir e.
 
So, 750 years, if a piece of money of that age came out, it
means the village is much older than that.

112
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Û şikeftên jî hene. Şikeftên vê ra dibên Şikeftên Hefter.
Heta hîn însanên tewr selef hatiye vir yanî şên kirî heye.
 
In the caves that exist. These caves are called Hefter. Even
in the past, ancient people came here, meaning there are
settlements.

113
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Û Şikeftê Benî Cewşe jî heye, û bitalî em bawer bikin ko ev
heft şikeftena maneto însanên meyî yanî dîrokî û ewelî da
vir şên kirine.
 
And there's also the cave of Beni Cewshe, and so we believe
that these seven caves mean that our historical and ancient
people settled here.

114
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Lê em, wan însana hinek hene dibên belkî însanên meyî, yanî
Herêma Efrînê kesek pirr nizane ku weleh am çend sal in
hatine.
 
But we, some people say that perhaps our people, I mean, no
one in the Afrin region knows much about it, they say, well,
we came a few hundred years ago.

115
00:10:55,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Na, baweriya min pê, Efrîn navê xwe yek heye Çiyayê Kurmênc.
Ew, heştê kî, yanî heştêyan ve.
 
No, in my belief, Afrin only has one name, Mount Kurmênc
(Kurd Dagh). That goes back to the 80s, I mean the 80s.

116
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Fe bitalî yanî kevn e, çiqas dîrokê kurdî heye li ser
Kurdistanê ve nê bitalî em jî wek wan in.
 
So it is old, as long as there is Kurdish history on
Kurdistan, so we are also like them.

117
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Belê, te gotin Çiyayê Kurmênc ev navê Efrîn, 100 sal ne
tiştek bû.
 
Yes, when you said Mount Kurmênc, this name of Afrin wasn't
anything 100 years ago.

118
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Gelek gundên Çiyayê Kurmênc, girêdayî Çiyayê Kurmênc, di
Bakurê Kurdistanê dikevinê.
 
Yes.

119
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Gelek gundên Çiyayê Kurmênc, girêdayî Çiyayê Kurmênc, di
Bakurê Kurdistanê dikevinê.
 
Many villages of Mount Kurmênc, tied to Mount Kurmênc, fall
in Northern Kurdistan.

120
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Dema ew sînor çêbû pirr gund jî, belkî 20 gund, an bêtir
bêtir, bi Bakurê Kurdistanê ketin. Ew jî girêdayî Çiyayê
Kurmênc in.
 
That's right.

121
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Dema ew sînor çêbû pirr gund jî, belkî 20 gund, an bêtir
bêtir, bi Bakurê Kurdistanê ketin. Ew jî girêdayî Çiyayê
Kurmênc in.
 
When that border was created, many villages too, maybe 20
villages, or more, now fall in Northern Kurdistan. They are
also tied to Mount Kurmênc.

122
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Rast e, rast e.
 
Right, right.

123
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Mamoste Mihemed, tiştek din ez ji te bipirsim.
 
Teacher Mihemed, let me ask you something else.

124
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Navê gundê we... wek milet, di gundê we da ye, lê derketin
derve jî. Wek Efrîn, navçeya Bilbilê, Reco...
 
Go ahead.

125
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Navê gundê we... wek milet, di gundê we da ye, lê derketin
derve jî. Wek Efrîn, navçeya Bilbilê, Reco...
 
The name of your village... as a people, you are in your
village, but there is also a departure outside. Like Afrin,
the district of Bilbil, Reco...

126
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Yanî te dît weke hûn ketin navbera du navçeyan da, Bilbilê û
Reco da. Milet derketiye li giştî li gundan heye.
 
You saw how you fell between two districts, Bilbil and Reco.
The people have left, it happens in all villages.

127
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Milet ji kevn da jî derketiye, û ji nêzîk da jî derketiye,
li her derkî hene. Malbatên Xelalka, li Badîna hene, li
Hemşelekê hene, li Ereban hene, li Qerababa hene, li pir
deran hene.
 
The people have left since ancient times, and they have also
left recently. They are everywhere. The families of Xelalka
are in Badina, in Hemshelek, in Ereban, in Qerababa, they
are in many places.

128
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Mesela li Şamê da erê li Şamê da hene, li Helebê hene, li
her derkî hene yanî şên kirine.
 
For example, in Damascus, yes they have been in Damascus for
a long time, they are in Aleppo, they are everywhere,
meaning they have settled.

129
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Yanî kesî barkirî Efrînê jî?
 
Do you mean those who moved to Afrin as well?

130
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:16,000
Barkirina Efrînê jî, bi tewr selef çûyîne Efrînê jî, kirîvên
gund bûn. Belkî deh mal kirîv hebûn li gund pê saz dikirin û
def dikirin û derketine Efrînê.
 
The moving to Afrin as well, originally those who went to
Afrin, were the village's musicians. There were maybe ten
families of musicians in the village, they made music with
saz and def, and they moved to Afrin.

131
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Ew zirnevan û def...
 
Those zurna and def players...

132
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Zirnevan û def, ev pir hebûn derketine.
 
Zurna and def players, there were many here and they left.

133
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Ew ji kîjan malbatê ne, kî ne?
 
Which ones, from which families are they, who are they?

134
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Malbatên Şehnik in, vê ra digotin malê Hemedê ne, malê
Reşûnê ne, malê Eftik in, malê Elî Çeçen e, evna malbatên
kirîvên gund bûn.
 
They are the families of Şehnik, they were called the house
of Hemed, the house of Reshûn, the house of Evdik, the house
of Eli Chechen, these were the families of the village's
musicians.

135
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Mamoste Mihemed, tiştek din ji te bipirsim.
 
Teacher Mihemed, let me ask you something else.

136
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Dema tu di Herêma Efrînê da bî, tu diçî kî derê, dibêjî
gotineke "Xelalkî". Ev çiye? Çi wateyê dide ev gotina?
 
Go ahead.

137
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Dema tu di Herêma Efrînê da bî, tu diçî kî derê, dibêjî
gotineke "Xelalkî". Ev çiye? Çi wateyê dide ev gotina?
 
When you are in the Afrin region, wherever you go, they say
a word "Xelalkî". What is this, why is this word said?

138
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Xelalkî, yanî wek dibêjî bervajkî. Şorekî rast be gerek
nerast be, û rast jî nerast be.
 
Xelalkî, it means, as you say, reversed. A word that is
right must be wrong, and the right must also be wrong.

139
00:12:52,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Em pirr dibihîsin bi vî gotinê. Bi xwedê, dîrokeke wê heye
lê ez naxwazim ez nav pirkî vekim, lê wisa wek...
 
We hear this a lot. By God, it has a history but I don't
want to open it up a lot now, but as it is...

140
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Yanî her tiştekî bervajkî dikin. Her gotinekî bervajkî
dikin.
 
You mean they do everything in reverse. They say every word
in reverse.

141
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Tebîeta miletê Xelalka gişk wisa dimînin, yanî ê bi hev ra
wek dibêje duzgun û ne duzgun.
 
The nature of the people of Xelalka is all like this,
meaning whether it is straight or not straight with each
other.

142
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Bi hev ra deng dikin yan deng nakin. Yanî ew jî adetek ne
xerab e. Em giş hewarî hevdu dikin.
 
Whether they talk to each other or not. I mean, that is also
not a bad custom. We all help each other.

143
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Malava be.
 
Bless your house.

144
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Malava te jî, û ser serê me, ser çavê me, ser dilê me re hûn
hatine gundê Xelalka.
 
Bless your house too, on our head, on our eyes, on our
heart, you have come to the village of Xelalka.

145
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Spasiya we jî dikim, û em gelek şa bûn bi hatina we.
 
I also thank you, and we were very happy with your coming.

146
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:51,000


147
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Bîra Seydê, li rojhilatê gund e. Û heta niha ava wê heye,
cotkar, şivan av xwe jê peyda dikin.
 
Seydê's well is located in the east of the village. It still
has water, farmers and shepherds get their water from it.

148
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Nêzî 300 xanî û bêtirî çar hezar kes di gund da hene.
Xelalka mezintirîn gundê Navçeya Bilbilê ye.
 
There are nearly 300 houses and more than four thousand
people in the village. Xelalka is the largest village in the
Bilbile district.

149
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Û gundê dawiyê ye girêdayî Bilbilê ye. Xelkên gundê Xelalka
debara jiyana xwe li ser çandiniyê dikin.
 
And it is the last village connected to Bilbile. The people
of Xelalka village make their living from agriculture.

150
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Û darên zeytûnan, behîv, kerez, rez, incas û hingivîn
diçînin. Her weha baxçeyên sebzeyan jî li ber bîr û kaniyan
diçînin.
 
And there are olive, almond, cherry, grape, plum, and honey
trees. They also plant vegetable gardens near wells and
springs.

151
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,000
Di gel wan zeviyên zad jî diçînin.
 
Along with them, they also plant crop fields.

152
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Xwedîkirina sewalên asta duyem de tê, mîna pez û bizin û
çêlek têne xwedîkirin. Û berhemên wan li bazarên Reco,
Meydana, Bilbilê û Efrînê têne firotin.
 
Animal husbandry comes in second place, like sheep, goats,
and cows are raised. And their products are sold in the
markets of Reco, Meydana, Bilbile and Afrin.

153
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Hin malbat jî mêşên hingiv jî xwedî dikin.
 
Some families also raise honey bees.

154
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:55,000


155
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Xelalka, gundê dawiyê navçeya Bilbilê, Kantona Efrînê ye.
 
Xelalka is the last village of the Bilbile district, Afrin
Canton.

156
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Heft kîlometreyî li rojavayê Bakurê navçeya Bilbilê,
 
It is located seven kilometers to the northwest of the
Bilbile district,

157
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:07,000
û çil û pênc kîlometreyî li bakurê bajarê Efrînê dikeve.
 
and 45 kilometers to the north of the city of Afrin.

158
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Navê gund ji peyva xel, ango tulbûna zinaran, ji ber ku gund
di kûpika çiyayekî zinarî da ava bûye.
 
The name of the village comes from the word xel, meaning the
peeling of rocks, because the village was built in the bowl
of a rocky mountain.

159
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Û di zivistanan da dema berf û baran dibariya, pê ra kevir
tul dibûn.
 
And in winter, when it snowed and rained, stones would peel
away with it.

160
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Nêrîneke din heye, dibêje ko ev tê wateya dengê avê.
 
There is another opinion, which says this means the sound of
water.

161
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Ji ber ku gund bi kaniya avê navdar bû.
 
Because the village was famous for its water spring.

162
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Gundê Xelalka, di kûpika Çiyayê Gazê da ye, ji aliyê bakur
ve ye.
 
Xelalka village is located in the bowl of Mount Gaze, on the
north side.

163
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Bilindahiya Çiyayê Gazê, 1100 metro ye. Ew jî berdewamiya
Çiyayê Gir e li Bilbilê ye.
 
The height of Mount Gaze is 1100 meters. This is also the
continuation of Mount Gir in Bilbile.

164
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Li bakurê gund geliye Meydankê yek e û digihîje bendava
Eşûnê û Çiyayê Gazê.
 
To the north of the village is the valley of Meydanke and it
reaches the Eshun dam and Mount Gaze.

165
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Li rojhilat gundê Elîbeg. Li başûr Qurnê û zinara çiya. Girê
Segrekê, Girê Gobîjê û Girê Kaniya Tava.
 
To the east is the village of Elibeg. To the south are Qurne
and mountain cliffs. Segreke Hill, Gobije Hill, and Kaniya
Tava Hill.

166
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Û li başûrê gund, Çela û Çiyayê Xewrekê dikevin.
 
And to the south of the village, Chela and Mount Xewreke are
located.

167
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:07,000


168
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Mamoste, te kengî dest bi karê wênesaziyê kiriye?
 
Teacher, when did you start painting?

169
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Valla di zaroktiya xwe da, dest pê kir, ji aliyê min da
şiyana resimkirinê ra hezkirina min jê ra hebû.
 
By God, it started in my childhood, from my side, I had an
ability and love for drawing.

170
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Ji ber wê jî tiştê min didît, min dixwest ez bikim form.
 
That's why whatever I saw, I wanted to shape it.

171
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Di wê hunerê da, bi resmên tabloyên ra, ew tişt di zaroktiya
me da çêbû.
 
In that art, painting pictures for tableaus, that's how
things started for me in my childhood.

172
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Di malbata te da kes, karê wênasaziyê dikir? Kesî ev kar
nedikir?
 
Was anyone in your family doing painting? Nobody was doing
it?

173
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Kesî kar nedikir, lê ez dikarim bêjim bavê min wek
hunermendekî bû.
 
No one worked on it, but I can say my father was like an
artist.

174
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Ji ber, berberî dikir, ji ber necarî dikir, ew tiştên nîgaşa
hunerî bi giştî wî jî hebû.
 
Because he used to do barbering, he used to do carpentry, he
also had the aspect of general art painting.

175
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Yanî wek tiştekî, te çi ji bavê xwe fêr bû?
 
So you mean, what did you learn from your father?

176
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Ez dikarim bêjim wek mînak, berwazên jê ra amade dikir, an
necarî dikir. Ev tişt, bêtir me jê girt.
 
I can say, for example, making frames, or doing carpentry.
We took these things from him more.

177
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Çawa tu formê tiştekê bidî, çawa cemaliyekê bidî tabloyê,
evna hemû me jê girtin.
 
How to give shape to something, how to give beauty to a
painting, we got all this from him.

178
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Te qaf jî çêkir yanî ev?
 
Did you also make frames, I mean, you?

179
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Erê me bi xwe jê dar wek berwaz çêdikir, em bi xwe jê wek
formên wisa me derxist.
 
Yes, we ourselves framed wood from it, we ourselves made
such forms out of it.

180
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Dema te dest pê kir, tu li gund bûyî, an tu derveyî gund
bûyî? Li bajêr bûyî?
 
When you started, were you in the village, or were you out
of the village? Were you in the city?

181
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Zaroktiya xwe da, dema ez diçûm dibistana seretayî, heta
refa şeşan ez li gund bûm. Lê piştre em derbasî Helebê bûn.
 
In my childhood, when I went to primary school, I was in the
village until the sixth grade. But after that we moved to
Aleppo.

182
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Heta refa nehê li, ji wê zêdetir, em hinekî pê ra nêzîktir
bûn û me tiştên wiha nas kirin. Di merheleya lîseyê da
(sanewî), bêtir em derbasî enstîtuya hunerî (mehedê finûn)
bûn.
 
Until the 9th grade we became more connected to it and we
recognized everything. In the secondary stage (high school)
we entered the institute of fine arts.

183
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Li Helebê... heta bekaloriyayê, me bi xwendinê re wisa dewam
kir evna jî. Lê, di xwendina bekaloriyayê da em qet, ev jî
wek tiştek neda naskirin li wê derê û min xwe qut kir.
 
In Aleppo... until my baccalaureate, we continued with my
studies. But when it came to the baccalaureate studies, I
stopped paying attention and I cut myself off from it there.

184
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Yanî bi giştî çend sal in tu vî karî dikî?
 
I mean generally, how many years have you been doing this
work?

185
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Ez dikarim bêjim di salên nav 93 û 94 da min dest pê kiriye,
heta 4-5 salan berê naha ez jê qut bûme ev e.
 
I can say I started in the years 93-94, until 4-5 years ago,
I'm now distant from it.

186
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:59,000
Min nedît, tu cîhekî tabloyên xwe nakî pêşangehekê?
 
I have not seen it, don't you have a place for your
paintings, an exhibition?

187
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:08,000
Belê, em dicivîn. Pêşangeh çêdibûn, cemaet çêdibûn û em
amade dibûn bi tabloyek, du tabloyan, carna sê tabloyên...
 
Yes, we would gather. Exhibitions happened, gatherings
happened and we got ready with one painting, two paintings,
sometimes three paintings...

188
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Bi giştî çend hunermendên Efrînê çêdibin em jî amade dibin.
 
Generally several artists of Afrin gather and we also get
ready.

189
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Lê tiştinên wisa yên şexsî û tenê, me bêtir nekiriye.
 
But such personal and individual things, we haven't done
much.

190
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:22,000
Em hewl didin ku tiştinên wiha jî çêbikin.
 
We are trying to do things like this too.

191
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:29,000
Mamoste, dema destpêkir, te çawa kir çi bû? Destpêkê ew
meraqa te çi bû?
 
Teacher, when you started, how did you do it? What was that
initial curiosity of yours?

192
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:38,000
Destpêkê me çi didît, ez di rêzên pêncan û şeşan da min hew
çêdikir, qazek, mirîşkek, darikê, tiştek wisa bû.
 
At the beginning, whatever I saw in the 5th and 6th grade, I
just drew a goose, a chicken, a piece of wood, or something
like that.

193
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,000
Me çi didît, dema em diçûn Helebê,
 
We saw what we saw, but when we went to Aleppo,

194
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Mamosteyê min ê hunerî, min karekî bêtir da xebatê, û min
bêtir dît. Min erebeya gund kirîbû resm. Di Helebê bêtir min
didît.
 
My art teacher paid more attention to me, and I saw it more.
I had kept the village carts in mind. I saw them more in
Aleppo.

195
00:18:52,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Wê demê min belkî pênc-çar tabloyên erebeyan bi xwe çêkir,
min gelek bêtir pêşkeftî kir ev tişt e.
 
At that time I made maybe 4-5 paintings of carts myself,
they were the things that progressed the most.

196
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Ez bêjim naha... di gundê Xelalka da, ez bêjim gerek wênesaz
tu her gav kar bikî.
 
I would say now... you are in the village of Xelalka, I
would say as a painter you should always be working.

197
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Ji ber ku hemû tişt li ber çavan e. Yanî tu cûda dibînî yek
traktorê diajo, tu şivanekî dibînî.
 
Because everything is right before your eyes. You see it
differently, one is driving a tractor, you see a shepherd.

198
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Ew dayik wek niha çawa nan çêdikin, tu nan dibînî. Çiqas
tiştekî baş e yanî.
 
That mother, like how they make bread now, you see the
bread. How good of a thing it is, I mean.

199
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Ez bêjim, gerek wênesaz tu car ji karê xwe dûr nekeve.
 
I would say a painter should never stay away from his work.

200
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:27,000
Û di kar da her wext bixebite, ji ber ku hemû tişt li ber
çavan in.
 
And in work always be working, because everything is before
the eyes.

201
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Ema dema tu di bajêr da bî, belkî tu tiştekî wiha nabînî, tu
tenê di televizyonan da dibînî.
 
But when you are in the city, maybe you don't see things
like this, you only see them on televisions.

202
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Di internetê da dibînî.
 
You see them on the internet.

203
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Lê di gund da hemû li ber çavan e. Kanî hene, dar hene,
şivan hene û cotkar heye.
 
But in the village everything is before the eyes. There are
springs, trees, shepherds, and farmers.

204
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Çawa dayik kar dikin, çawa diçin ji kaniyê avê tînin, ev
hemû wêne ne di rastiyê da.
 
How mothers work, how they go fetch water from the spring,
these are all true paintings.

205
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Belê hemû wêne ne, her tişt li ber çavan in. Her însanek
dikare li wê derê bi jiyana xwe da bibîne.
 
Yes they are all paintings, everything is before the eyes.
Any person can see that in their life.

206
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Her wext ev tiştên hunerî dikare li ber xwe da wisa di
jiyana xwe da bibîne...
 
Every time these artistic things can be seen in front of you
in your life...

207
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Ji aliyekî din, ew reng û hunera vê cihêbûnê bi alemeke
bedew da naskirin.
 
On the other hand, he introduced the color and art of this
distinctiveness to a beautiful world.

208
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
Wekî mînaka vê tabloyê.
 
Like the example of this painting.

209
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Ku ev tablo ji folklorê me yê Kurdî ye.
 
That this painting is from our Kurdish folklore.

210
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Ji xwarinê û çawa nan çêdikirin bi vî şeklî.
 
From eating to how they made bread, in this way.

211
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Ji dema kevanî, ku tu mînak wî, pisîkê çawa dîtiye, li derî
dinihêrî.
 
From the time of the housewife, for instance, how he saw the
cat looking at the door.

212
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Demê tiştên me yê poxan e, çawa li ser sêlê nan tên kirin.
 
When it's our puff pastry, how they are made on the saj.

213
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Li ser textik nan tê pehnkirin.
 
The bread is flattened on the wooden board.

214
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Heta tîroka destê wê da ji dar tê çêkirin.
 
Even the rolling pin in her hand is made of wood.

215
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Ev tiştên hemî folklorê, da tu dûrî wê hatî, tu di wêneyekê
de tînî dikişînî û bi alemekê didî naskirin.
 
All these folklore items, since you came far from them, you
bring them into a picture and introduce them to a world.

216
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Huner jî ew tişt e ku tu tînî der.
 
Art is the thing that you bring out.

217
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Mamoste ev wêne, yanî ji bîra te hat ber çavên te û te
çêkir, yan te li derekê dîtî ye te wêne kişandiye û te ev
tablo çêkiriye?
 
Teacher, this picture, I mean did it come from your memory
to your eyes and you made it, or did you see it somewhere
and took a picture and made this painting?

218
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
Yanî, ev ne ji xeyala te derketiye?
 
I mean, this didn't come out of your imagination?

219
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Na na ji xeyala min ne derketiye, bes ji gundekî bakur ku
min wêneya wî dîtiye.
 
No, no, it didn't come out of my imagination, only from a
northern village whose picture I saw.

220
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:11,000
Her cilekî vê dayikê, yê bakur e? Yanî bakurê Kurdistanê ye?
Yan ev tişt hemî kurdî ne?
 
Every cloth of this mother, is it of the north? I mean, of
Northern Kurdistan? Or are all these things Kurdish?

221
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Taybetî ne cilê Efrînê ye?
 
They aren't specifically Afrin clothes?

222
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Na taybetî cilê Efrînê tu nikarî bêjî e, wekî cilê Efrînê ye
wekî tu dikarî bêjî yê Kurdistanê têde hatiye temsîlkirin.
 
No, you can't say it's specifically Afrin clothes, it's like
Afrin clothes, like you can say Kurdistan is represented in
it.

223
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Mînak text e, mînak meqes ye, mînak ta ye, mînak lastîk e,
mînak agirdan e, ev hemî di her qada Kurdistanê de têde tê
bikaranîn.
 
For example the board, for example the scissors, for example
the thread, for example the rubber shoes, for example the
hearth, all these are used in every region of Kurdistan.

224
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Mamoste tu çi herî te çêkirî û di bîra te de derneketiye û
ew jî tişta ku tu hîn çêdikî?
 
Teacher, what is the thing you made the most and it hasn't
left your memory, and it's also the thing you are still
making?

225
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:58,000
Di pirtûkan me çêkir, tiştê herî balkêş, ên di dawiyê me
çêkir, belkî we jî dîtiye li ser rûpela min jî heye. Sureta
serokatiyê ya li ber bilbilê.
 
We made it in books, the most interesting thing we made
recently, maybe you have seen it, it's on my page too. The
picture of the leader by the nightingale.

226
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
Çend caran wêneyê te çêkiriye?
 
How many times have you made the picture?

227
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:10,000
Du caran min çêkir. Cara dawî wekî me çêkir, min wilo di
dilê xwe de me çênekir, ji ber rewşa hewayê û ew rewşa
zivistanê û ba û bahozê ew carekî xerab bû.
 
I made it twice. The last time we made it, I didn't make it
from my heart, because of the weather conditions, the winter
conditions, the wind and storms, it got ruined once.

228
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Dîsa min texmîn kir, min çêkir, me got belkî em tiştekî wekî
wî mezin dîsa çêbikin. Sîh metreyî bi bîst metreyan wêneyekî
wisa mezin ew bû. Yanî ez dikarim bêjim wêneyê herî mezin ê
li Kurdistanê hatî çêkirin em dikarin bêjin ew e.
 
I guessed again, I made it, we said maybe we can make
something as big as that again. Thirty meters by twenty
meters, that was such a big picture. I mean, I can say it's
the biggest picture made in Kurdistan, we can say it's that.

229
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,000
Mamoste em zehf spas dikin. Em serkeftinê ji te re dixwazin.
 
Teacher, we thank you very much. We wish you success.

230
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:50,000
Spas dikim ser çavan re spas dikim.
 
Thank you, on my eyes, thank you.

231
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Ehmedê Qoço, wekî dengbêj û tembûrvanekî kevnar e.
 
Ehmed Qoço, is like an ancient dengbêj (traditional singer)
and saz player.

232
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:58,000
Wî gelek stranên dengbêj Îbrahîmê Tirko digot.
 
He used to sing many songs of the dengbêj Ibrahim Tirko.

233
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:01,000
Hemze Beko mamosteyê zimanê kurdî yê yekem bû.
 
Hemze Beko was the first Kurdish language teacher.

234
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Wî li ber destê mamoste Reşîd Hemo fêrî zimanê kurdî bû.
 
He learned the Kurdish language under the tutelage of
teacher Reşid Hemo.

235
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Û gelek kes fêrî kurdî kir, û di warê ziman de xebateke
mezin meşandin.
 
And he taught Kurdish to many people, and carried out great
work in the field of language.

236
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:16,000
Ji ber vê yekê gelek caran ket zindanên dewleta Sûriyê.
 
Because of this he was imprisoned many times by the Syrian
state.

237
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:25,000
Bîlal Mihemed Kose, wekî zimanzan û di heman demê de zavayê
helbestvanê mezin Cegerxwîn e.
 
Bilal Mihemed Kose, is a linguist and at the same time the
son-in-law of the great poet Cegerxwin.

238
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Wî gelek pirtûk nivîsîne. Mîna bend û şîret, bend û pend.
 
He has written many books. Like verses and advice, verses
and proverbs.

239
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Mamoste Mihemed Şêx Qember, yek ji rewşenbîrên destpêkê di
kantona Efrînê de ye.
 
Teacher Mihemed Şêx Qember, is one of the first
intellectuals in the Afrin canton.

240
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:45,000
Wî li gelek dibistan û herêmî karê mamostetiyê kiriye û di
warê kurdewariyê de xwe gelekî bi pêşxistiye.
 
He worked as a teacher in many schools and regions, and
developed himself a lot in the field of Kurdish culture.

241
00:23:45,000 --> 00:24:02,000
Rêjeya xwendinê di gund de bilind e, piranî ji wan
bawernameyên zanîngehê di beşên curbecur de standine, û her
waha gelek xwendekar jî xwendina xwe berdewam dikin.
 
The literacy rate in the village is high, most of them have
obtained university degrees in various departments, and also
many students continue their studies.

242
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Nema wext o delalê min î malê.
 
There is no time left, my dear of the house.

243
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:12,000
Peyabo ez herim bişînim tatî hatî, dîna min î delalê min î
malê.
 
Come so I can go see until you come, my crazy one, my dear
of the house.

244
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:17,000
Çûyî şeka wer kîsa dîtina ber pê ya delalê min î malê, ev
asriqê herîrî.
 
You went, doubting in the pocket, seeing before the feet, my
dear of the house, this silk market.

245
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:21,000
Got ma dîtina ber qaba, delalê min î malê, tu tînî, emîr
Şêxî.
 
She said did you see in front of the door, my dear of the
house, you bring, Emir Sheikhi.

246
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:32,000
Go qehokê dest xweda mero xalo, qunaxoka nan dixwazin.
 
She said uncle give your hand, they want a stopover of
bread.

247
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:37,000
Belê îro em li gundê Xelilka ne, navê derbasî cem dayîka
bûne.
 
Yes, today we are in the village of Xelilka, we have entered
the mother's place.

248
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Navê wê jî dayîka Hecîra ye.
 
Her name is Mother Hecira.

249
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:45,000
Dayîkê jî xwest, leçerê çêbikin, bastîqê çêbikin, destên
dayîka sax bin.
 
The mother also wanted to make fruit preserves, make bastiq
(grape leather), bless the mother's hands.

250
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:47,000
Merheba ji we re dayê.
 
Hello to you, mother.

251
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

252
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:49,000
Em destpêkê we nas bikin.
 
Let's get to know you first.

253
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Navê min Hecera, ehlen we sehlen, ser çavên me tu hatî.
 
My name is Hecera, welcome, you came on our eyes.

254
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,000
Sax be. Em te jî nas bikin?
 
Bless you. Can we get to know you too?

255
00:24:56,000 --> 00:25:01,000
Navê min Kîbar e, ehlen we sehlen, em pir kêf xweş bûn ku tu
hatî cem me ser çavan.
 
My name is Kibar, welcome, we were very happy that you came
to us, on our eyes.

256
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:03,000
Ser çava.
 
On my eyes (You're welcome).

257
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:07,000
We wextê xwe li me girt, em pir kêf xweş bûn ku hûn hatin
derbasî cem me bûn.
 
You took your time for us, we were very happy that you came
and visited us.

258
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:11,000
Spas ji we re, em jî kêf xweş in ku em derbasî cem we bûn,
dayê navê te em zanibin?
 
Thank you, we are also happy that we visited you, mother,
can we know your name?

259
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,000
Elîf.
 
Elif.

260
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:13,000
Ser çava.
 
On my eyes.

261
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:15,000
Destên te sax bin.
 
Bless your hands.

262
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:17,000
Û yên te sax bin.
 
And bless yours.

263
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:27,000
Me behsa leçer kir û we behsa gelek tiştan kir, ka hinekê ji
me re bêje, hûn çi leçer, leçerê çi çêdikin?
 
We talked about fruit preserves and you talked about many
things, tell us a bit, what fruit preserves do you make?

264
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:31,000
Weleh leçer em yê kundirê reş çêdikin.
 
Well, we make preserves from black pumpkin.

265
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:34,000
Yê mişmişan em çêdikin.
 
We make it from apricots.

266
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Yê kundirê misrî çêdikin.
 
We make it from Egyptian pumpkin.

267
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:38,000
Yê tiriyan çêdikin.
 
We make it from grapes.

268
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:40,000
Yê hêjîran çêdikin.
 
We make it from figs.

269
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:48,000
Û gava ku em çêbikin wextê em çêbikin pir be, em nakin
qutiyan. Em didin cîranên xwe dikin tên, nexweş em çêdikin.
 
And when we make it, if we make a lot, we don't put it in
boxes. We give it to our neighbors, the sick, we make it.

270
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:57,000
Em dihûrin yek em difirkin... şerbeta xwe serî dixe.
Bihîvkên xwe em lê didin dikelînin çêdikin înşelleh.
 
We chop it up, we rub it... boil its sherbet. We add our
almonds to it, boil it, make it, hopefully.

271
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:59,000
Yanî hûn her tiştî leçera wî çêdikin?
 
Meaning you make preserves out of everything?

272
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:04,000
Tiştê hazir nîne an em bi destê xwe çêdikin.
 
Is there anything ready-made or do we make it with our own
hands.

273
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:09,000
Wê tişta herî baş dema hûn çêdikin, ew gund dema jin radibin
e û didin alîkariyê.
 
That best thing when you are making it, in that village when
the women get up and help.

274
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:18,000
O weleh dikarin ku yê min pir be wek leçer e yan her tiştekî
din, em didin e hevdu, em hevdu dikin arîkar.
 
Oh, by God, they can if I have a lot like preserves or
anything else, we give it to each other, we help each other.

275
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:20,000
Niha jî wextê hejîran e?
 
And is it the time for figs now?

276
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:25,000
Nika dema hêjîran e, doh sê çar jin hatine min gote min
arîkar bikin me leçer çêkir.
 
Now is the time for figs, yesterday three or four women
came, I told them to help me, we made preserves.

277
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,000
Destên we sax bin.
 
Bless your hands.

278
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,000
Yên te jî sax bin.
 
Bless yours too.

279
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:37,000
Dayê ez tiştekî ji te bipirsim weke pirs, niha ez nizanim,
niha leçera hûn dê çawa vî çêbikin leçera hêjîran?
 
Mother, let me ask you something as a question, now I don't
know, how will you make this fig preserve now?

280
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:40,000
Em avê di serî didin, şekir dikinê.
 
We put the water on top, add sugar to it.

281
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Helekê dide kelê, em hêjîran dikinê. Çîçek leymûnê jê
dikinê. Bîvê qut dikinê em dikelînin.
 
Once it starts boiling, we add the figs. We add a little
lemon to it. We chop almonds, we boil it.

282
00:26:46,000 --> 00:27:00,000
Sor dibe, em dadixînin... Ew dema kelê, tu çawa kel e, te
şûşt, ew kel dibe. Ew bi xef em bi destê xwe de didin xwarin
em dihûrin, bi xeyb piçûk dibe, ew leçer amade dibe fêkiyan.
 
It gets red, we take it down... That boiling time, how it
boils, you washed it, it boils. Secretly, we feed it with
our hands, we chop it, secretly it gets smaller, that
preserve gets ready for fruits.

283
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:01,000
Hûn xîçik hîdikin dema...
 
You make it a little when...

284
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Û sor dibe, me hilandin jibo zivistanê yanî wextê zivistanê
te divê. Bixwe zivistanê me çi çêkir em heta zivistanê em
hilînin.
 
And it gets red, we kept it for winter, meaning for winter
time you want it. Eat it in winter, whatever we made, we
keep it until winter.

285
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:09,000
Lê çer her tiştekî yê leçerî pir e na?
 
But does everything make a lot of preserves, no?

286
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:15,000
Lê çer her tiştek yê leçerî pir nînin. Hejîr e, zebeş e,
bihok e, kundir e, cure tişt pir in em çêdikin di cehên wek
vî de, didin e hevdu.
 
But not everything makes a lot of preserves. Figs,
watermelon, quince, pumpkin, there are many kinds of things
we make in places like this, we give to each other.

287
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:17,000
Ên baştir şîrîn, yên tirş, wextê tirî... Em wextê... yê wî
çêdikin, heye tiştan hene.
 
The better sweet ones, the sour ones, when it's grape... We
when... make his, there are, there are things.

288
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:19,000
Mînak tu bibêjî tu bes ji hejîran çêdikî?
 
For example if you say, do you only make from figs?

289
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:29,000
Na, ez ne ji bihokan, tiştê amade pirr in ji tiştên min
digot ê hejîr, ên gundan... wextê ku te hejîr... tiştên
zeytûnê...
 
No, I don't from quinces, the ready things are many from the
things I said, figs, the villages'... when you have figs...
olive things...

290
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Ez bêjim tu wê çawa çêbikî hûn hînik amade dikin?
 
Let me ask, how will you make it, are you preparing a
little?

291
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:34,000
Em avê jê re dikin... Emê ava wê û ya wî.
 
We add water to it... We will add its water and his.

292
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Wê pêşî hazir bike, em hînik dînê wexta tu amade bikî ka tu
dê çawa çêbikî.
 
Prepare it first, we will look a bit when you are preparing
it, how you will make it.

293
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Erê emê hazir bikin. Tiştên mezin le hejîr.. le hejîre ah me
kir... ev hejîr in hejîr... ax nîn e ah... nîn e... ah ev,
eh em ê hinekê bikin ser.
 
Yes we will prepare it. The big things fig preserves.. fig
preserves ah we did it... these are figs, figs... there
isn't ah... there isn't... ah this, eh we will add a bit.

294
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:47,000
Ev wek leçer hûn wisa datînin ser, bes paşî ku te çêkir...
 
Like preserves you put it on like this, but after you made
it...

295
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:49,000
Naxwe pêşî bastîq... Em pêşî bastîqa xelîr çêdikin.
 
So first bastiq... We first make clear bastiq.

296
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Hûn bastîqê çawa çêdikin?
 
How do you make bastiq?

297
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:59,000
Em bastîqê li ser agir, em didin ser ê... şorbeya wi em li
ser datînin... Em avê lê dikin e, nîvî de didin kêlê.. Û
paşî em şekir wî lê dikin e... ard em lê dikin û derdikin e.
 
We put bastiq on the fire, we put it on... we put its soup
on... We put water on it, let half of it boil.. And then we
put sugar in it... we put flour and take it out.

298
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:08,000
Em de didin kelîn, heya tu dibînî sor dibe. Dîsa em radikin
hînik sar dibe, em didin tebsî, da hîşk bibe nêzîka hev.
 
We let it boil, until you see it turns red. Again we take
it, it cools down a bit, we put it on trays, to dry close
together.

299
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:11,000
Ev bastîq hûn weke tenê ji tirî çêdikin?
 
This bastiq, do you make it just from grapes?

300
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:29,000
Na, hin car em ji tirî, ev bi rojên yek.. wextê mişmişên
hebe, hin caran jê re mişmiş dixin... Saet em we ji behîvan
tu her tişt. Lê piranî me bi tenê tişt e, tişt me qet in
wisa dibînin, em wî jê re dikin... Piranî.
 
No, sometimes we make it from grapes, this is on certain
days.. when there are apricots, sometimes we put apricots
for it... Sometimes we do it from almonds, you every thing.
But mostly it's just one thing, things we never cut them
like this, we do it for him... Mostly.

301
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:30,000
Destên te sax bin.
 
Bless your hands.

302
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Yên we jî sax bin.
 
Yours too.

303
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Emê derbasî cem dayê jî bibin... wele hûn gelek tişt.
 
We will go to the mother's place too... well you many
things.

304
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:37,000
Tu çi leçer... bastîq çêdikî tu nika?
 
What preserves... what bastiq are you making now?

305
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:41,000
Lê ke bastîq çêkin nîko... nika em pêşî hejîran... me
hurîskirin..
 
But they will make bastiq... now we first figs... we mashed.

306
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:45,000
Em nika de rêxin ser kîsik û suzgêvek û... bişkên...
 
We will now spread it on a bag and a strainer and... smash
it...

307
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Pişt re amade dikim dixim suzgê... min daxiste xwe da.
 
Afterwards I prepare it, put it in the strainer... I put it
down.

308
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Wê hazir amade be ev yê me... ev min de kir, me derbazî...
wî de kir weke ard e. Em hewle didin serî... ez ê yek wek wî
jî dekim de... Ewê wê re xînin dako ew we re hej bibe.
 
That will be ready, this of ours... I did this, we passed
it... put it like flour. We try on it... I will put one like
it... We will spread it out so it shakes you.

309
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:55,000
Pênc rojek em radin nav pelan, em ê bînin mal, teva hev
kirin ew.
 
We keep it in the leaves for five days, we will bring it
home, mix it all.

310
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:58,000
Çawa didin li ser wê bastîqê, hûn sizmîş dikin tiştî ew wek
tişta te...
 
How do you put it on that bastiq, do you squeeze the thing,
it like your thing...

311
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:05,000
Na me hazir kirine... na te em sizdikim.. ev ev me sizkirî..
me av û rûn... û ew, suzgêv re da. Ew em yê didin nika em ê
daxînin em ê pê şirînkin.
 
No we prepared it... no we squeeze it... this, we squeezed
this.. we water and oil... and that, gave it to the
strainer. That we are putting now, we will take it down, we
will sweeten it with it.

312
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Em ê de raxînin daku ew qîçk hişk bibe. Em bînin mal em ê we
behîvê em tehlîhev dikin, tu xistî, em ê ji we re pirtik
dikin bînin...
 
We will spread it out so it dries a little. We bring it home
we will with the almonds, we mix it, you put it in, we will
cut it into pieces for you and bring it...

313
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:15,000
Û hûnê dema daxin... sîrê?
 
And when you take it down... the garlic?

314
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:24,000
Em ê neylonekê de raxînin, ên nav re... me nav qemîşek weke
ard min raxistiye tu... ev nav e... em ê daxînin yek dî wek
wî serê me. Ew der raxistin... wek wilo hîşk bibin. Me derê
raxistin, paşê em çêkin...
 
We will spread it out on a nylon, in it... we spread a reed
like flour... this is inside... we will take down another
one like it on top of us. Spreading it there... so it dries
like that. We spread it there, then we make...

315
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:28,000
Em ê bînin bi wê bikin û we re ev hişk bibin tişt tiştin qat
e... ew çend wisa em qat dikin ji xwe ew dibin hev. Em dixin
nav wê re din e.
 
We will bring it and make it with it and for you these will
dry things things layer... we fold it like that a few times
and they come together themselves. We put it inside and give
it.

316
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:31,000
Heta biharê zivistanê, tiştek nabe yê wan...
 
Until spring, winter, nothing happens to them...

317
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:33,000
Wexta zivistanê çi di...
 
What in winter time...

318
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Em we derxînin ji we der, ê em derxînin... fêkî û gûz nav me
we dirxist tişt weke bîv... û em ê ji xwe nîşan bidin û
didin mêvanan.
 
We bring it out for you, we bring it out... fruit and
walnuts inside we took out things like almonds... and we
will show it ourselves and give it to the guests.

319
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:43,000
Hûn tiştê hazir nîn e ku amade...
 
Don't you have something ready that's prepared...

320
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:52,000
Weleh ê hazir e tişta me... ev ev hejîr e me... nîn e nika
fêkî yan tişta min amade bû ye ev çû min dît xelas bû ye bîv
min nîn e nika nemaye... hîn deşt e dî...
 
By God, the ready one is our thing... this, this fig is
ours... there's no fruit now or my thing is prepared, this
went I saw it's finished I don't have almonds now there's
nothing left... it's still outside again...

321
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:54,000
Sê roja çêkî hûn ber tavê de din?
 
Do you put it in the sun for three days to make it?

322
00:29:54,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Sê ro, dudu di ro we, tiştî em dikin û der tînin paşê em
dikişînin jê re diqetînin û dikin yek... Em sê wek wan. Qat
dibin, nîvqat em tiştên wê radikin dikin cî...
 
Three days, two in the sun you, we do things and take it out
then we pull it, cut it and make it one... We three like
them. They fold, half fold we pick up its things and put
them in a place...

323
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:01,000
çi tiştên zivistanê be,
 
Whatever winter supplies there are,

324
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:04,000
wextê zivistanê hat, em ê derxin
 
when winter comes, we will take them out,

325
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:07,000
û em ê dîsan mîna tiştê havînê bixwin.
 
and we will eat them again just like summer food.

326
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:09,000
Vêca bastîqê tirî hûn çêdikin?
 
So, do you make grape fruit leather (bastîq)?

327
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:11,000
Em bastîqê çêdikin, kewsanê,
 
We make fruit leather, we make kewsan,

328
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:18,000
hejîran, bastîq, em ê gişî çêkin. Zivistanê em ê bixin ber
hev,
 
figs, fruit leather, we make them all. We will gather them
in the winter,

329
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:21,000
û wextê ku qesidî, mêvanek ji me re hat, em ê pê hesilînin.
 
and when a guest visits us, we will serve it to them.

330
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:24,000
Ev tiştên zivistanê ne.
 
These are winter supplies.

331
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:27,000
De... vêca hûn çawa çêdikin?
 
So... how do you make them?

332
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Ka ji min re bêjin çawa?
 
Can someone tell me how you used to...

333
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:32,000
Em çawa çêdikin?
 
Should I tell you how we make it?

334
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:33,000
Erê ji min re çawa çêdikî?
 
Yes, how do you make it for me?

335
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:34,000
Berê?
 
About the figs?

336
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:36,000
Ji berê ve...
 
About the figs, yes.

337
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:39,000
Eh, ji berî we de, hûn çawa çêdikin bastîq û zehterê?
 
Eh, from the old days, how do you make the fruit leather and
other things?

338
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Erê, em berê de çêdikin.
 
Yes, we make it the traditional way.

339
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Em ê hejîrên xwe bînin, em ê rind hişk bikin, em ê di
baniyan rakin,
 
We bring our figs, we dry them well, we put them on the
roof,

340
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:48,000
û em ê dîsa jî bînin xwarê.
 
and then we bring them down again.

341
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:51,000
Em ê dîsa ava wê çêkin serî.
 
We prepare their syrup first.

342
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:55,000
Sûdê tê kin, paşê zeytê tê kin û kelê pê bînin.
 
We add milk, then we add oil and boil it with them.

343
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Bînin darxînin, hişk bikin.
 
We take them out and let them dry.

344
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Zivistanê jî em ê paşê hildin.
 
And then in the winter, we store them.

345
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:03,000
Navê wî çi ye?
 
They remain for winter. What is its name?

346
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Hejîrên hişk.
 
Dried figs.

347
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:07,000
Hejîrên hişk. Hûn jê re dibêjin hişk.
 
Dried figs. You call them dried?

348
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:09,000
Erê. Em hejîrên rind hişk bikin.
 
Yes. We dry the figs well.

349
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:13,000
Di baniyan ra dikin, paşê jî ji hev hişk dibin,
 
We put them on the roof, then they dry completely,

350
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:17,000
em dibin, paqij dikin. Kelê, sûdê tê kin,
 
we take them inside and prepare them. We add boiling water
and milk,

351
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:21,000
zeytê tê kin... kelê pê were, ha zû, paşê darxin hişk bibin.
 
we add oil... we boil it with them quickly, then put them
out to dry.

352
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:23,000
Û em dihilînin.
 
And we store them.

353
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:24,000
Mîjo jî?
 
What about mîjo?

354
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Mîjo jî wekî mîjo çêdibe.
 
Mîjo is also made similarly.

355
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:27,000
Wekî mîjo...
 
Like mîjo...

356
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:31,000
Ew jî wekî mîjo, mîjo jî dîsa tenê tirî ye.
 
That is also like mîjo, mîjo is again just grapes.

357
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:35,000
Em tînin, dikelînin... Ev e mîjo, em nakelînin.
 
We bring it, we boil it... This is mîjo, we don't boil it.

358
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:37,000
Ew mîjo, em natêkin kelê.
 
We don't boil that mîjo.

359
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:39,000
Evî sar da dibin radixînin.
 
We take it outside in the cold and spread it out.

360
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:42,000
Heta hişk be, hefteyekê dimîne. Em mîjo radikin.
 
We leave it for a week until it dries. Then we put the mîjo
away.

361
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:45,000
Mîjo bi wî rengî ye.
 
Mîjo is exactly like that.

362
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:47,000
Na, te fêkiyên din navêje nav, wek hejîr?
 
No, you don't add other fruits, like figs?

363
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Na navêjine, na tenê hejîr in.
 
No, we don't, it's just figs.

364
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:53,000
Hejîrên me ne mîjo ye, safî hejîr e.
 
Our figs are not mîjo, they are pure figs.

365
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:55,000
Na, bi qasî destpêkirin...
 
No, regarding how you start it...

366
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Em dikin, wekî din çêdikin...
 
We do it, we make it like the rest...

367
00:31:57,000 --> 00:31:58,000
De destê we sax be.
 
May your hands be blessed.

368
00:31:58,000 --> 00:32:02,000
Û dayê, tu xweş bi gundê xwe dizanî? Tu gundî yî...
 
And mother, you know your village well? You are a
villager...

369
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:04,000
Erê...
 
Yes...

370
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:08,000
Di gundê we de berê kaniyên avê li ku derê bûn? We av ji ku
dianî?
 
Where were the springs located in your village in the past?
Where did you get water?

371
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Kanî pir bûn. Em diçûn Kaniya Elmêsê,
 
There were many springs. We used to go to Elmês Spring,

372
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:14,000
em diçûn kanî... em diçûn Meydanê...
 
we used to go to the spring... we went to Meydan...

373
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:19,000
Em bi dewarên xwe diçûn dihanî, 4-5 kanî li pêşiya gund
hebûn.
 
We went with our livestock and brought it, there were 4-5
springs in front of the village.

374
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:24,000
Em diçûn bi dewarên xwe karê xwe dikir. Me cilên xwe
dişûştin bi wan kaniyan,
 
We went with our livestock to do our work. We washed our
clothes at those springs,

375
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:30,000
me darên xwe av didan. Em diçûn ku bi sîtil û tenekeyan av
dihanî.
 
we watered our trees. We used to go and bring water with
buckets and cans.

376
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:35,000
Gund gihîştinek hebû... Jinan tenekeyên avê li ser serê xwe
dikişandin...
 
Reaching the village was far... The women used to carry cans
of water on their heads...

377
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:38,000
Niha av nemaye kêm bûye. Me kaniyên tijî dîtine,
 
Now the water is gone, it has decreased. We used to see full
springs,

378
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:42,000
jin derdiketin ser kaniyê da tijî bikin. Me kanî didît tijî
bûn.
 
women went to the springs to fill up. We would see the
springs full.

379
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:44,000
Ew kanî dûr in nexwe?
 
So those springs are far?

380
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Dûr in, erê. Li pêşiya gund e, dûr in.
 
They are far, yes. They are far in front of the village.

381
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:51,000
Kanî hebû ku dido-sê saet diçûn. Heta gihîştana wê avê dîsa
wext derbas dibû.
 
There was a spring that took two to three hours to reach. It
took time to reach that water.

382
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:52,000
Miletek pir hebû?
 
Were there many people?

383
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:58,000
Dema milêt pir hebû. Ew gundî bûn. Em bixwe jî diçûn.
 
There were many people back then. They were villagers. We
went ourselves too.

384
00:32:58,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Bes li geliyekî mezin bûn Meydanê bi dar.
 
But there was a large valley called Meydan with trees.

385
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:03,000
Ev derên han hemû dar bûn,
 
All these places were covered in trees,

386
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:08,000
Meydan, darên mêwan da, darên çilikan, darên sêvan danîn,
 
Meydan was filled with vineyards, olive trees, and apple
trees,

387
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:12,000
darên geliyan... deşta fere bû. Lê niha av tune ye, av kêm
e.
 
the trees of the valleys... the plain was vast. But now
there is no water, water is scarce.

388
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:15,000
Niha ziwa ye, av tune ye.
 
Now it is dry, there is no water.

389
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:19,000
Bîr pir in. Zivistanê baran zivistanê be kêm av e.
 
There are many wells. In the winter it rains, but water is
scarce in winter.

390
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:22,000
Heta naha jî bîr nizm bûne.
 
Even now the wells are low.

391
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:42,000
De nexwe, destê we sax be û spasiya we dikim.
 
Well then, bless your hands, and I thank you.

392
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:05,000
Em ê destê xwe bidin xebatê, wextê ku derkeve em ê dinav de
dînin...
 
We will get to work, when it's ready we will put it
inside...

393
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:07,000
Destê we sax bin. Spas ji we re.
 
May your hands be blessed. Thank you.

394
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,000
Spas ji we re jî.
 
Thank you too.

395
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:13,000
Dayê tu tiştekî dixwazî bêjî de kerem ke? Destê we sax be.
Tevî we em sipas dikin.
 
Mother, if you want to say something, please go ahead. May
your hands be blessed. We thank you all.

396
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:27,000
Spas ji we re jî.
 
Thank you as well.

397
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:32,000
Gundê Xelalka, bi kevirên xwe yê navdar e.
 
The village of Xelalka is famous for its stones.

398
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:37,000
Li derdora wê gelek cûreyên keviran lê hene, û gelek rengên
keviran têne dîtin.
 
There are many types of stones around it, and many colors of
stones can be found.

399
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Ev hemû cûre, li hemû dever û parêzgehên Sûriyê dihatin
şandin.
 
All these varieties were sent to all regions and provinces
of Syria.

400
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Lê mixabin ev hemû avahiyên gund bi keviran hatine avakirin.
 
Unfortunately, all the buildings in the village were built
with stones.

401
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:52,000
Kurmikî, weke bazareke kevnar li bakurê rojavayê gund e.
 
Kurmikî is like an ancient market in the northwest of the
village.

402
00:35:52,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Têde gelek şikeft û sarnîç hene, ku ew kurhî ya dîroka vî
bajarokî diyar dike.
 
There are many caves and cisterns inside it, showing the
deep history of this town.

403
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:07,000
Qatê Qîzikê, weke deriyekî gundî bi ber bi sorda li bakurê
rojavayê gund e.
 
Qatê Qîzikê is like a village gate leading out to the
northwest of the village.

404
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:14,000
Sê goristanên gund hene: Şêxil, Şêx Îs û Kaniya Mala.
 
There are three cemeteries in the village: Şêxil, Şêx Îs,
and Kaniya Mala.

405
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:20,000
Û miriyên gund li Şêx Îs û Kaniya Mala tên veşartin.
 
And the dead of the village are buried in Şêx Îs and Kaniya
Mala.

406
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:23,000
Gundê Xelalka bi pirbûna kaniyên avê navdar e.
 
The village of Xelalka is famous for its abundance of water
springs.

407
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:27,000
Derdora şêst û çar kanî û bîrên avê lê hene.
 
There are around 64 springs and water wells there.

408
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Ji wan kaniyan: Kaniya Tawê li rojavayê gund.
 
From those springs: Tawê Spring in the west of the village.

409
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:35,000
Kaniya Mala, Kaniya Axzûtikê, li başûr Kaniya Gozê,
 
Mala Spring, Axzûtikê Spring, in the south Gozê Spring,

410
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:42,000
Kaniya Belek, Mehmedko, Şêx Reşîd, Çirçirkê, Tizbiyê û
herwiha kaniyên din jî hene.
 
Belek Spring, Mehmedko, Şêx Reşîd, Çirçirkê, Tizbiyê, and
there are other springs as well.

411
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:45,000
Geliya Golmirê: Li başûrê rojavayê gund e.
 
Golmirê Valley: It is in the southwest of the village.

412
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:49,000
Bêhtirîn hemû gundiyan meydanê: elem dara, çaxmaxa,
 
Most of all the villagers in the square: elimdara, çaxmaxa,

413
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:55,000
cela, çençeliya, çaxmaxa, bi çol, kurizê elîçan kûm dibûn.
 
cela, çençeliya, çaxmaxa, in the wilderness, they would
gather at the plum bushes.

414
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:58,000
Jiber pirbûna avê di wî geliyî de.
 
Because of the abundance of water in that valley.

415
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:05,000
Lê niha ew kêm bûye. Jiber sedemên guhertina rewşa
keşûhewayê û pirbûna bîrên nûjen.
 
But now it has decreased. Due to the changing weather
conditions and the abundance of modern wells.

416
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:10,000
Belê mam ji min re, em ji gund derketin... nahajî em
gihîştine kê derê?
 
Yes uncle, we left the village... where have we arrived now?

417
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:13,000
Ziyaretek e, jêre dibêjin Şêx Elt.
 
It is a shrine, they call it Şêx Elt.

418
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:14,000
Şêx Elt?
 
Şêx Elt?

419
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:15,000
Şêx Elt...
 
Şêx Elt...

420
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:19,000
Ev, ziyaretekî menşûr e, kevn e...
 
This is a famous, ancient shrine...

421
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:24,000
Eva berî sed salî, heştê salî, heftê salî...
 
This is from a hundred, eighty, seventy years ago...

422
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:29,000
Pezê me nexweş dibû, 5-6 meryan datanîn keriya pez.
 
Our sheep would get sick, 5-6 people would bring the flock
of sheep.

423
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:37,000
Li dor wê ziyaretê digerandin. Digerandin sê neqla.
 
They would walk them around that shrine. They would circle
it three times.

424
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:38,000
Yanî, tirbeyek heye?
 
So, is there a tomb?

425
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:40,000
Meqamê şehîdekî ye.
 
It is the shrine of a martyr.

426
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:41,000
Meqamê şehîdekî ye...
 
It's the shrine of a martyr...

427
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:48,000
Meqamê şehîdekî ye, belê... Diçûn cem, ew cihê welî ye, yanî
cihê şehîd...
 
It is the shrine of a martyr, yes... They would go to it, it
is a holy place, meaning a martyr's place...

428
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:54,000
Navê wî cihê Şêx Xelîl, yanî Şêx Elt.
 
The name of the place is Şêx Xelîl, meaning Şêx Elt.

429
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:55,000
Şêx Elt.
 
Şêx Elt.

430
00:37:55,000 --> 00:37:57,000
Yanî kurmancî em dibêjin Şêx Elt.
 
So in Kurmanji we call it Şêx Elt.

431
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:03,000
Aha... Datanîn li dorê ziyaretê sê neqlan digerandin?
 
Aha... You would bring them and circle the shrine three
times?

432
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:09,000
Û paşê sibê, ranedibûn... Axek ji wir wek tevekekê
werdigirtin.
 
And then the next morning, they wouldn't just leave... They
would take some dirt from there like a handful.

433
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:18,000
Tevli avê dikirin, dibirin heta li ser wî pezê nexweş
direşandin. Ew pezê nexweş rehet dibû.
 
They would mix it with water and sprinkle it on those sick
sheep. Those sick sheep would heal.

434
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:22,000
Û wê derê de hene... mesele yekî serî êşiyaye, an tiştek
din.
 
And in that place... for example, if someone's head hurt, or
something else.

435
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:31,000
wek ku dibêjin siza heye, tê paçekê, kincê xwe girê didin.
Hema çi nexweşî hebe rahet dibe.
 
Like they say there is a penalty, they come and tie a cloth,
a piece of their clothing. Whatever sickness they have is
cured.

436
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:35,000
Û ez da te pirs bikim, ev a... behsa kevirê qîzikê dikin, ka
ev kevirê li kû derê ye ew kevir?
 
And let me ask you, this... they talk about the girl's
stone, where is that stone?

437
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:37,000
Kevir li wê jor e, kevirê ziyareta ye.
 
The stone is up there, it's the shrine's stone.

438
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:38,000
Li jora we ye, ewa wisa?
 
It's above you, like that?

439
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:41,000
Yanî, ew ax e... ew tiştekî wisa.
 
I mean, it's dirt... it's something like that.

440
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:43,000
Em dikarin wî kevirî bibînin?
 
Can we see that stone?

441
00:38:43,000 --> 00:38:46,000
Ev dera ku em tên axê jê dibin, ewa ye.
 
This place we come and take dirt from, that is it.

442
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:52,000
Tirbelik dibin? Ew, li kûderê ye? Pêşiya me ye, li jor?
 
Do you take it from a small tomb? Where is it? In front of
us, up there?

443
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:56,000
Cihê wek çavê qîzikê ye... wek cismê qîzikê ye.
 
The place is like a girl's face... like a girl's body.

444
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:58,000
Nîşana xuriyê avî ye, wek nexweşiya çerm...
 
It's a cure for water scabies, like a skin disease...

445
00:38:58,000 --> 00:39:05,000
Nexweş dibin, wek nexweşiya xuriyê dertê. Qîzik çawa cemed
dibe ji tirsa? Ew jî...
 
They get sick, like an itch breaks out. How does the girl
freeze from fear? It's like that...

446
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:10,000
Û qenaeta milet heye, ew qenaet e.
 
And the people have faith, it's a belief.

447
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:11,000
Bawerî ye?
 
It's a belief?

448
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:15,000
Belê bawerî ye, wekî baweriya te pê hat, tu pê dihesî...
 
Yes, it's a belief, if you put your faith in it, you'll feel
it...

449
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:17,000
Zaro wê rehet bibin, gava zaro nexweş dibin?
 
Children will be healed when they get sick?

450
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:21,000
Erê gava zaro nexweş dibin, xuriya avî li çermê wan tê...
 
Yes, when children get sick, they get water scabies on their
skin...

451
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:23,000
Em li wir ber ava wê ziyaretê dibin...
 
We bring them to the water of that shrine...

452
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:24,000
Yanî hûn axê jê dibin?
 
I mean, you take the dirt from it?

453
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:29,000
Em axê jê dibin... em tînin, destê wan lê didin... nîşana wî
cismê qîzikê dehl in.
 
We take the dirt from it... we bring it and rub their hands
with it... the mark of that girl's body is smooth.

454
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:30,000
Hûn pereyan jî tê datînin?
 
Do you put money in it too?

455
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:33,000
Û perê jî... wextê em axê dibin, em peran datînin...
 
And money too... when we take the dirt, we put money...

456
00:39:33,000 --> 00:39:44,000
Em perê dikin wir, wextê şivanek an yekî ji wir derbas bibe,
dikare pereyan bibe? Na, qedexe ye, tu destê xwe jê nakî.
 
We put the money there, when a shepherd or someone passes by
there, can they take the money? No, it's forbidden, you
don't touch it.

457
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:48,000
Wextê tu wê pereyê datînî, xêra xwe datînî, kes wê nabê...
eger yek bibe dê xerc bike, nabe...
 
When you put that money, you leave it as charity, nobody
takes it... if someone takes it and spends it, they
shouldn't...

458
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:50,000
Carna zaroyên bi xuriyê nexweş dibin têne wir?
 
Do children sometimes get sick with that itch and come here?

459
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:56,000
Zaroyên ku di gundekî de ew xurî li wan tê, ew dertên ber
ziyareta wê qîzê,
 
The children in a village who get that itch, they come to
the shrine of that girl,

460
00:39:56,000 --> 00:40:00,000
ji wir axê tînin, paşê tu destê xwe pê didî rehet dibin.
 
they bring dirt from there, then when you rub it on them,
they heal.

461
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:01,000
We xwe di êş û derdan de xistiye?
 
Did you put yourselves in pain and suffering?

462
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:05,000
Na, me xwe di êş û derdan de nexistiye, em li kûçkê xwe
rûniştine.
 
No, we didn't put ourselves in pain and suffering, we are
sitting in our room.

463
00:40:05,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Bes gund gişt dîtî ye.
 
But the whole village has been seen.

464
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:10,000
Erê, gund gişt dîtî ye, dibêjin ofîsa xelkê tuneye.
 
Yes, the whole village has been seen, they say there is no
public office.

465
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:11,000
Spas, spas, serkeftin.
 
Thank you, thank you, good luck.

466
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:31,000
Serkeftin, serkeftin.
 
Good luck, good luck.

467
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:54,000
Mala te ava be, saet xweş.
 
Bless you, well done.

468
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:55,000
Sazbenda, saet xweş be.
 
Musicians, well done.

469
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:56,000
Saet xweş, erê.
 
Well done, yes.

470
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:59,000
Belê, li vir jî em ê xatirê xwe ji we bixwazin.
 
Yes, here we will bid you farewell.

471
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:01,000
Li vir jî em digihîjin dawiya bernameya xwe.
 
Here too we reach the end of our program.

472
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:03,000
Îro jî em li gundê Xelalkoyê bûn.
 
Today as well, we were in the village of Xelalko.

473
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:05,000
Heta hefteyeke din em ê dîsa bi hev re bin.
 
Until next week, we will be together again.

474
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:07,000
Bi bernameyek din bi xatirê we.
 
With another program, goodbye to you.

475
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:09,000
Gidî qîzê, mala bavê...
 
Oh girl, the father's house...

476
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:14,000
Ya lê qîzê xelkê ye.
 
Oh the daughter of the people.

